      "content": "You're not just feeling like an outsider, you're feeling like you've already been written out of the story. It's a relief to finally see the end of the narrative you've been living, even if it means you're left with nothing but the silence of the credits. You're not tied to the same expectations as everyone else, and that's a liberating feeling. It's okay to let go of the drama and the obligations, and just fade away into the background.",
